{
  "hub": {
    "id": "bp-analytical-data-platform",
    "category": "blueprint",
    "name": "Analytical Data Platform",
    "description": "A complete blueprint for an analytical data platform (data warehouse / lakehouse). Includes core systems, EARS requirements, fitness functions, and architecture decisions. Import all or select individual elements.",
    "tags": [
      "data",
      "analytics",
      "warehouse",
      "lakehouse",
      "reporting",
      "etl",
      "governance"
    ],
    "requiredMetamodel": "c4-ddd-governance-builtin"
  },
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "bp-adp-sys-ingestion",
      "type": "system",
      "label": "Data Ingestion",
      "description": "Collects raw data from operational systems, third-party APIs, and event streams. Handles batch and streaming loads.",
      "technology": "Apache Kafka / Airbyte",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 60,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 220,
      "collapsed": false
    },
    {
      "id": "bp-adp-sys-storage",
      "type": "system",
      "label": "Data Lake / Warehouse",
      "description": "Stores raw, curated, and aggregated data. Supports both schema-on-read (lake) and schema-on-write (warehouse) patterns.",
      "technology": "Snowflake / Delta Lake / BigQuery",
      "x": 500,
      "y": 60,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 220,
      "collapsed": false
    },
    {
      "id": "bp-adp-sys-transform",
      "type": "system",
      "label": "Transformation Layer",
      "description": "Applies business logic, cleansing, and aggregation rules to produce analytical datasets. Supports incremental and full-refresh models.",
      "technology": "dbt / Spark",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 340,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 220,
      "collapsed": false
    },
    {
      "id": "bp-adp-sys-serving",
      "type": "system",
      "label": "Serving / BI Layer",
      "description": "Exposes curated datasets to business users via dashboards, embedded analytics, and self-service query tools.",
      "technology": "Power BI / Looker / Superset",
      "x": 500,
      "y": 340,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 220,
      "collapsed": false
    },
    {
      "id": "bp-adp-req-latency",
      "type": "requirement",
      "label": "Ingestion Latency",
      "ears_type": "ubiquitous",
      "action": "deliver all streaming events to the data lake within {{INGESTION_LATENCY_SECONDS}} seconds of generation",
      "templateParams": [
        {
          "key": "INGESTION_LATENCY_SECONDS",
          "label": "Ingestion latency (seconds)",
          "hint": "60",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": "60"
        }
      ],
      "priority": "must",
      "status": "draft",
      "rationale": "Near-real-time data enables operational dashboards and timely alerting.",
      "x": 940,
      "y": 60,
      "width": 200,
      "height": 80,
      "collapsed": false
    },
    {
      "id": "bp-adp-req-quality",
      "type": "requirement",
      "label": "Data Quality Gate",
      "ears_type": "ubiquitous",
      "action": "reject or quarantine any record that fails schema validation or referential-integrity checks before loading into the curated zone",
      "priority": "must",
      "status": "draft",
      "rationale": "Prevents propagation of bad data into analytical models and dashboards.",
      "x": 940,
      "y": 180,
      "width": 200,
      "height": 80,
      "collapsed": false
    },
    {
      "id": "bp-adp-req-access",
      "type": "requirement",
      "label": "Role-based Access",
      "ears_type": "ubiquitous",
      "action": "enforce column- and row-level security based on the viewer's organisational role, with no exceptions",
      "priority": "must",
      "status": "draft",
      "rationale": "Sensitive financial and personal data must not be accessible to unauthorised roles.",
      "x": 940,
      "y": 300,
      "width": 200,
      "height": 80,
      "collapsed": false
    },
    {
      "id": "bp-adp-req-lineage",
      "type": "requirement",
      "label": "Data Lineage",
      "ears_type": "ubiquitous",
      "action": "record full column-level lineage for every transformation and expose it through the catalogue API",
      "priority": "should",
      "status": "draft",
      "rationale": "Lineage is required for regulatory audits and enables trust in analytical outputs.",
      "x": 940,
      "y": 420,
      "width": 200,
      "height": 80,
      "collapsed": false
    },
    {
      "id": "bp-adp-ff-freshness",
      "type": "fitness-fn",
      "label": "Data Freshness Guard",
      "description": "Verifies that each critical dataset in the warehouse is refreshed within its SLA window. Alerts on-call if a model has not run within the agreed interval.",
      "category": "operational",
      "automated": true,
      "trigger": "continuous",
      "threshold": "All critical models refreshed within their SLA (default: {{FRESHNESS_SLA_HOURS}} h)",
      "templateParams": [
        {
          "key": "FRESHNESS_SLA_HOURS",
          "label": "Dataset freshness SLA (hours)",
          "hint": "4",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": "4"
        }
      ],
      "status": "active",
      "x": 1200,
      "y": 60,
      "width": 180,
      "height": 52,
      "collapsed": false
    },
    {
      "id": "bp-adp-ff-quality",
      "type": "fitness-fn",
      "label": "Data Quality Score",
      "description": "Runs dbt tests or Great Expectations suites after each transformation run. Fails the pipeline and alerts if the pass-rate drops below threshold.",
      "category": "operational",
      "automated": true,
      "trigger": "on-deploy",
      "threshold": "Test pass-rate ≥ {{QUALITY_PASS_PCT}}%",
      "templateParams": [
        {
          "key": "QUALITY_PASS_PCT",
          "label": "Data quality test pass-rate (%)",
          "hint": "99",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": "99"
        }
      ],
      "status": "active",
      "x": 1200,
      "y": 130,
      "width": 180,
      "height": 52,
      "collapsed": false
    },
    {
      "id": "bp-adp-ff-cost",
      "type": "fitness-fn",
      "label": "Query Cost Guard",
      "description": "Tracks cloud warehouse credit consumption per team/project. Blocks scheduling of ad-hoc queries that would exceed the daily budget.",
      "category": "holistic",
      "automated": true,
      "trigger": "continuous",
      "threshold": "Daily spend ≤ {{DAILY_BUDGET_CAP}} per team",
      "templateParams": [
        {
          "key": "DAILY_BUDGET_CAP",
          "label": "Daily warehouse budget cap per team",
          "hint": "1000",
          "defaultValue": "1000"
        }
      ],
      "status": "proposed",
      "x": 1200,
      "y": 200,
      "width": 180,
      "height": 52,
      "collapsed": false
    },
    {
      "id": "bp-adp-adr-storage",
      "type": "adr",
      "label": "ADR-001: Lakehouse over pure DWH",
      "status": "accepted",
      "date": "2024-01-15",
      "context": "The organisation needs to support both structured reporting (SQL/BI tools) and unstructured / ML workloads on the same data. A traditional relational DWH cannot cost-effectively store raw JSON, image metadata, or large model artefacts.",
      "decision": "Adopt a lakehouse architecture (Delta Lake / Iceberg open table format on object storage) as the primary storage layer, with a semantic layer (Snowflake / BigQuery) for curated, high-performance analytical queries.",
      "consequences": "Teams can run ML experiments directly on raw data without ETL. Storage costs decrease vs a full DWH copy. Governance requires careful management of open-format schemas and compaction jobs.",
      "alternatives": "1. Pure cloud DWH (Snowflake only) — simpler but expensive at ML scale. 2. Hadoop-based data lake — mature but operationally heavy.",
      "x": 1200,
      "y": 280,
      "width": 180,
      "height": 52,
      "collapsed": false
    },
    {
      "id": "bp-adp-adr-transform",
      "type": "adr",
      "label": "ADR-002: dbt as transformation standard",
      "status": "accepted",
      "date": "2024-02-03",
      "context": "Multiple teams write transformation logic in ad-hoc SQL scripts, Spark jobs, and stored procedures. Lack of version control, testing, and documentation creates data trust issues.",
      "decision": "Standardise all curated-zone transformations on dbt (data build tool). All models must have at least one schema test and a description. Spark is permitted for raw ingestion and heavy ML feature engineering only.",
      "consequences": "Improved lineage, automated testing, and documentation. Learning curve for teams unfamiliar with dbt. CI/CD pipeline required for model deployment.",
      "alternatives": "1. Custom Spark jobs — more flexible but no built-in lineage or testing conventions. 2. Stored procedures — tightly coupled to warehouse vendor.",
      "x": 1200,
      "y": 350,
      "width": 180,
      "height": 52,
      "collapsed": false
    }
  ],
